From 0baaa6ad088ae0650a062a06890edc938f86ab32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sudharsan <rajusudhar1616@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Apr 2026 23:41:15 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(generator): add oneOf/anyOf discriminated union support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace the silent `interface{}` fallback for OpenAPI `oneOf`/`anyOf`
with an idiomatic Go sum-type representation:

* New `GoUnion` / `GoUnionVariant` model in `src/utils/go-types.ts`
  alongside a `'union'` variant on `GeneratedType`.
* `generateUnionTemplate()` in `src/templates/go-templates.ts` emits
  a marker interface, one struct per variant with a marker method
  (`func (Variant) isUnion() {}`), and — when
  `discriminator.propertyName` is present — a `<Union>Wrapper` with
  `UnmarshalJSON` that switches on the discriminator value.
* `createGoUnion()` in `src/generator/go-generator.ts` derives variant
  names from `title` (or synthesizes `<Union>VariantN`), respects
  `discriminator.mapping` to label cases, and threads `encoding/json`
  + `fmt` imports automatically.
* Wired `'union'` into both `single` and `category` file organizers.
* New fixture `tests/fixtures/discriminated-union.yaml` covering
  discriminated `oneOf`, plain `anyOf`, and scalar `oneOf` variants.
* 6 new tests in `tests/generator/discriminated-unions.test.ts`
  (suite total 121 tests).

Why: `oneOf`/`anyOf` previously degraded to `interface{}`, losing
type identity and forcing consumers to handle JSON dispatch by hand.
This is the first slice of `feat-discriminated-unions` (Phase 2);
remaining work — non-discriminated unmarshal dispatch, mapping when
variant titles are absent, nested `oneOf` inside `allOf` — is tracked
in the feature plan.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
